    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create a Python script that consumes one message from a managed subscription or queue, I will use Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) as the concrete external provider. This choice is based on the requirement to use a specific external provider and make it identifiable in the code. The script will import the necessary AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) and use it to interact with the SQS service. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887747398,
          "start": 1789887744154
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd9f889a0012seLUBOmUao0JD",
